  "boundaries": [
    "This checker allows equal edge heights, and the notes lower-than-origin phrase must not become strict<.",
    "The four-half-unit headroom is relative to source edge, not destination floor or an actor body-height parameter. The crossed-layer byte5 accesses are verified arithmetic; no stronger geometric meaning than the source is inferred.",
    "Blocked uses finite sentinel0xff. Do not replace it with infinity; wide byte-domain cases can select that numeric height and later fail the occupancy/collision check. No claim these cases occur on retail maps.",
    "Edge coefficient is masked to two bits0..3; notes listing only0/1/2 do not establish rejection or clamping of3.",
    "Only valid directions0..3 supplied by the parent are covered. Invalid direction falls through without initializing shift registers; no deterministic fallback is claimed.",
    "The helper has no RNG, live movement, HP/fall damage, pending-flag or effect-bit writes. Parent and later resolution own those stages.",
    "Failure does not clear previous fall-height/target work. Successful child writes can survive later parent depth/slope/surface rejection.",
    "Current flat admitted behavior is unchanged; layered/slope/fall/mount/terrain expansion remains guarded/deferred."
  ],
